That's because of your assistance!

258
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:52,237
My speed and jumping abilities have
been doubled due to our combined power!

259
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,200
An alien!

260
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,760
Just my luck!

261
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,740
What the hell is going on here?!

262
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:17,380
Hey, you really can't see this?

263
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:20,490
Huh?

264
00:15:20,573 --> 00:15:21,720
He can't see it.

265
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,340
He's not a stand user.

266
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:25,858
Then where did his powers come from?

267
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:27,520
What the hell are you?

268
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,320
You are a stubborn one.

269
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:31,917
As I've been trying to
tell you, I am an alien.

270
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,647
Fine, just give me a second.

271
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:37,357
Look, no offense, but it's hard
to wrap my head around all this.

272
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:40,260
Anyway, I truly appreciate your saving me.

273
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:44,777
Sirens are mundane here, but the
people on my planet abhor the sound.

274
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,801
The wavelength is very upsetting.

275
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:48,937
I'd like to repay that kindness.

276
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:51,432
It's the least I can do for one so brave.

277
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,060
Shall I turn into a fan for you?

278
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:57,817
Or perhaps a backscratcher to
grab those hard-to-reach places?

279
00:15:57,900 --> 00:16:01,841
I didn't get you out of there
because I wanted something in return!

280
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:07,737
But if you'll really do anything,
well, who am I to turn you down?

281
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:09,526
What is it you request of me?

282
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:12,537
First off, can you really
turn into anything?

283
00:16:12,620 --> 00:16:14,738
Like big or small or even multiples?

284
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:17,511
Yes, I can transform into nearly anything.

285
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:21,958
However, becoming complex machinery
or powerful objects is unfeasible.

286
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:23,657
I read you loud and clear,

287
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:26,457
and I can tell that we're going
to be the best of friends.

288
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:28,760
So you want to thank me, right? Yes.

289
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:33,197
Well, you're in luck, because I just
cooked up a brilliant idea, friend.

290
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:37,160
Trust me, it's a win-win for
everyone. Win-win? Right!

291
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:42,617
See, a few weeks ago, I won quite a bit
of spending money in the local lottery.

292
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:46,582
My mom found out about it, made a
big stink, and froze my account.

293
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:50,217
Once that woman makes up her mind
about something, your fate is sealed.

294
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:54,124
Being flat broke during the summer
is the worst, let me tell you.

295
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:59,720
That's why I need you to turn into these!

296
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:01,210
Can you?

297
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:04,780
What are they exactly?

298
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:06,809
A pair of dice, obviously!

299
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,877
And I'm gonna make some cash with them.

300
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:12,097
After that, I'll split the winnings
with you, thus creating a win-win.

301
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:14,500
So how do the dice function? Explain.

302
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:17,177
Wait, you really don't know what dice are?

303
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:18,780
I don't. My apologies.

304
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:21,241
There's nothing to apologize for.

305
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,960
It's super easy to learn.

306
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,612
I'll show you the ropes.

307
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:28,251
Anyone who likes playing games
goes nuts over these things.

308
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:31,077
They've got six sides and are
made from a hard material.

309
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:33,717
The red dot represents
the number one and the

310
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:36,197
other faces have different
numbers up to six.

311
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:37,110
I see.

312
00:17:37,193 --> 00:17:38,377
It's starting to make sense.

313
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:41,017
The five dots represent
the number five, correct?

314
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:41,977
That's right, Mr.

315
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:42,890
Alien!

316
00:17:42,973 --> 00:17:44,237
And three dots represent a three.

317
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:45,150
Yup!

318
00:17:45,233 --> 00:17:46,063
Now try turning into one!

319
00:17:46,146 --> 00:17:46,976
I'm at your service.

320
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:49,170
Simple.

321
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:53,906
It's close, but you're a little
too big to pass for a real die.

322
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:55,315
This is more like it.

323
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:57,325
You've also got an extra five.

324
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,757
Each face has a different
number from one to six.

325
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:03,157
The number's on one side, and
its opposite should equal seven.

326
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,400
Oh, my apologies.

327
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:07,880
Is this better?

328
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,317
That tickles something.

329
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:14,957
Hey, knock off the laughing.

330
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:17,300
And dice aren't supposed to talk. Huh?

331
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:18,780
Oh, come on.

332
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:20,220
I'll try harder.

333
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:23,160
I'm a little nervous about this, but...

334
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:26,580
You look good. Make that great.

335
00:18:26,700 --> 00:18:28,037
We can pull this off.

336
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:29,740
I'm getting all fired up!

337
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:33,257
Hope you're ready to lose
some cashola, Rohan Kishibe!

338
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:34,170
Can't breathe!

339
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:37,300
Wow, what a surprise.

340
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:41,560
Now why would Josuke
Higashikata be visiting me?

341
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:44,015
This is certainly out of the ordinary.

342
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:46,440
Did you uncover any more dirt on Kira?

343
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:50,117
Nope, nothing since the last
time we checked in with you.

344
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:51,580
So, uh, yeah.

345
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:54,237
Are you all done with your
manga work for the day?

346
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:58,317
I was wondering if you'd let me take
a peek at the next volume early.

347
00:18:58,400 --> 00:18:59,230
Hmm.

348
00:18:59,313 --> 00:19:01,254
What kind of nonsense are you scheming?

349
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:02,655
Spit it out, come on.

350
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:04,474
I should have figured.

351
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:07,280
Can't get anything past you, Rohan-sensei.

352
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,621
Kay, you got me.

353
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:10,329
I have an ulterior motive.

354
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:13,460
I'm begging you, sensei!

355
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:15,220
Please play Soul with me!

356
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:17,300
That's it? Soul?

357
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:19,404
I'm gonna be completely honest.

358
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:23,317
Summer's finally here, and
I'm totally strapped for cash.

359
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,377
Well, I do have $30,000 on hand.

360
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:28,931
This is all the money I've got
to my name, but it won't do.

361
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:30,650
Nowadays,

362
00:19:30,733 --> 00:19:32,517
30,000 yen won't get
you more than a couple

363
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:35,247
visits to the amusement
park and some snacks.

364
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:38,360
So I either make some
dough or go flat broke.

365
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:42,677
Taking risks and thrill-seeking is
the very foundation of being young.

366
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:44,257
That's what I think at least.

367
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:45,575
You agree, don't you?

368
00:19:48,260 --> 00:19:49,580
Let me be frank.

369
00:19:49,780 --> 00:19:51,997
I've despised you from
the moment I met you.

370
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:54,157
There's absolutely no
reason for me to waste

371
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:56,577
my precious time playing Soul with you.

372
00:19:56,660 --> 00:19:58,000
I guess you're right.

373
00:19:58,340 --> 00:20:00,697
I mean, you're not
exactly hurting for cash.

374
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:02,357
I don't know what I was thinking.

375
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:04,297
Why would you want to play a game with me?

376
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:07,960
Even so, count me in. Huh?
Seriously? You'll do it?

377
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:09,640
I don't dislike games.

378
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:10,937
In fact, I'm intrigued.

379
00:20:11,020 --> 00:20:12,957
Come around back whenever you're ready.

380
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:15,628
We're gonna have a great
time, Rohan-sensei.

381
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:21,197
Do these rules work for you?

382
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:24,420
Yeah, looks good each chip
is worth a thousand yen,

383
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:29,500
and you must roll three dice into the
bowl if one falls out you lose Got it.

384
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:30,710
All right.

385
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:32,397
I'll place the rules here.

386
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:33,557
So they're in plain view.

387
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:34,797
Okay, let's get this party.

388
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:35,710
Wait

389
00:20:38,060 --> 00:20:40,597
We won't be using those dice. Huh?

390
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:41,820
We'll use these.

391
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:43,777
They're a set I found in the house.

392
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:44,690
Oh

393
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,710
Really?

394
00:20:45,793 --> 00:20:46,623
That's interesting.

395
00:20:46,706 --> 00:20:49,157
Is there some reason that you
don't want to use my dice?

396
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:51,777
Not really I feel inclined to play with my

397
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:54,677
own is all just a whim
when I mentioned I was!

398
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:59,617
Intrigued it wasn't by the prospect
of playing Soul no no Josuke I was!

399
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:04,657
Intrigued by the prospect of swiping
30,000 yen from you now when you lose!

400
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:08,557
Against me I expect you to pay in full I
don't care how much we've been through!

401
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:09,600
Understand?

402
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:16,550
Perfect!

403
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:19,132
The dice he found are actually the alien!

404
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:23,197
I managed to sneak them into his
house when he wasn't paying attention!

405
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:24,660
I'm such a bad boy.

406
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:29,640
It won't be a ton, but you're about
to fund my summer Fugo, Rohan-sensei!

407
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:33,261
Now then, shall we determine
who gets to go first?

408
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:35,530
Four.

409
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:38,230
Yes!

410
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:41,000
Looks like you're up first. Roll the dice.

411
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:42,930
Ow!

412
00:21:43,013 --> 00:21:43,843
Ow, ow, ow!

413
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:46,420
I banged my hand into the table!

414
00:21:49,900 --> 00:21:52,640
Place your bet and roll
the dice. Yeah, right.

415
00:21:52,980 --> 00:21:56,380
Uh, guess I'll start things
off by betting 2,000 yen.

416
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:58,226
So I'll throw down two chips.

417
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:00,000
Alright, so will I.

418
00:22:00,180 --> 00:22:04,000
If I roll a one, a two, and a
three, I'll have to pay double.

419
00:22:04,160 --> 00:22:06,857
So I need to avoid those
numbers at all costs.

420
00:22:06,940 --> 00:22:10,180
One and two and three, keep
those rolls away from me!

421
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:17,100
The first roll calls for a light
touch, sort of like a practice toss.

422
00:22:18,020 --> 00:22:19,380
Here we go. Gently.

423
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:22,440
Okay, looking good!

424
00:22:24,300 --> 00:22:25,130
What?

425
00:22:25,860 --> 00:22:26,960
It's an omen!

426
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:31,420
Triple sixes, aka an omen!

427
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:34,260
Josuke wins five times what he wagered!

428
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:36,660
Hey, don't start that way, dumbass!

429
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:38,997
What I meant to say was...

430
00:22:39,080 --> 00:22:40,977
I can't believe I had such dumb luck!

431
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:42,997
A triple six and five times the winnings?

432
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:44,217
How's that even happen?

433
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:48,771
To the untrained eye, it almost looks
like I'm cheating even though I'm not!

434
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:54,555
Somehow, you already managed
to win 10,000 yen from me.

435
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:56,387
At any rate, let's continue.

436
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:58,800
If I'm not mistaken, I'm next.

437
00:22:59,060 --> 00:23:02,097
I want to get back what
I've lost, so I think...

438
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:03,780
I'll wager 10 chips.

439
00:23:04,780 --> 00:23:06,077
You sure about this?

440
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:07,360
And here we go.

441
00:23:11,540 --> 00:23:14,020
A one, a two, and a three.

442
00:23:14,460 --> 00:23:17,157
Rohan must pay double
the amount of his wager.

443
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:19,217
He's taken the hustle way too far.

444
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:20,535
It's getting obvious.

445
00:23:20,860 --> 00:23:24,120
Does this alien know the
meaning of the word restraint?

446
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:29,080
Shit, biscuits.

447
00:23:29,460 --> 00:23:31,872
If this keeps up, he'll bust us for sure.
